[Desktop Entry]
{{!--
  Handlebars template for the launcher entry in a flavored `.deb` and
  AppImage, selected by `bundle.linux.deb.desktopTemplate` in the config
  `build-flavor-tauri-config.mjs` writes. The trunk keeps tauri-bundler's
  built-in template, so a stock Buzz built from this repo ships exactly the
  desktop entry it always has.

  This is a Handlebars comment, not a `#` one, so none of it reaches the
  installed file. It sits after the group header rather than before it so the
  rendered output starts with `[Desktop Entry]` on line 1 whatever the
  renderer does with the surrounding newline.

  The bundler supplies `name`, `exec`, `icon`, `categories`, `comment` and
  `mime_type`. `categories` is deliberately unused, and is the reason this
  file exists: Tauri maps each `bundle.category` it knows to a single
  freedesktop token, and the closest one — `SocialNetworking` — maps to
  `Network;` alone. A chat app belongs under `Network;InstantMessaging;` too,
  and no category value produces it.

  `StartupWMClass` uses `{{icon}}` rather than `{{exec}}`: both are the main
  binary name, but `exec` is quoted when it contains a space, and a WM_CLASS
  is matched literally — a quoted one would never match the window, and the
  launcher would show a second generic icon beside the running app. The two
  are identical today because `demo-build-config.mjs` derives the binary name
  from a slug that cannot contain a space; this keeps them identical if that
  ever changes.

  `%u` is not in the built-in template, and without it the `MimeType` line is
  decoration: `xdg-open buzz-demo-…://…` would launch the app with no
  argument and drop the link. The app reads the URL out of `argv` (the
  single-instance handler in `lib.rs`), and an ordinary launch expands `%u`
  to nothing.
--}}
Type=Application
Version=1.0
Name={{name}}
{{#if comment}}
Comment={{comment}}
{{/if}}
Exec={{exec}} %u
Icon={{icon}}
StartupWMClass={{icon}}
Terminal=false
StartupNotify=true
Categories=Network;InstantMessaging;
Keywords=chat;messaging;team;projects;agents;nostr;
{{#if mime_type}}
MimeType={{mime_type}}
{{/if}}
